1.2.2 - Sunday 1 November 2026
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

Security fixes from zetacomponents/Webdav pull request #8, contributed by
Ekkehard Doerre (CJW Network), and pull requests #6 and #7:

- Renamed: The package is now se7enxweb/expcomponents-webdav (repository
  github.com/se7enxweb/expcomponents-webdav). It replaces
  se7enxweb/zetacomponents-webdav and zetacomponents/webdav, so existing
  requirements keep working; the class names (ezcWebdav*) are unchanged.

- Fixed: Paths can no longer leave the root of ezcWebdavFileBackend. Both
  path factories remove "." and ".." segments (RFC 3986, section 5.2.4),
  also from the Destination header of COPY and MOVE and after a URI
  fragment is attached. The file backend refuses request URIs and
  destinations that still contain such segments, also percent-encoded,
  with 403 Forbidden.
- Fixed: ezcWebdavFileBackend checks the real path (realpath()) of every
  resource it reads, writes, lists, copies or deletes, so a symbolic link
  inside the root that points outside of it, or a symbolic link whose
  target does not exist, is no longer followed: requests through such a
  link are refused with 403 Forbidden, collection listings leave it out,
  a recursive COPY does not copy it and a recursive DELETE is refused
  rather than following it. Symbolic links that stay inside the root keep
  working.
- Fixed: Request bodies with a document type declaration are refused with
  400 Bad Request, before and after parsing, and are parsed with
  LIBXML_NONET. The libxml error handling state is restored on errors.
- Fixed: Digest authentication compares the digest in constant time and
  sends a nonce from random_bytes().
- Fixed: Lock tokens are created from random_bytes() as UUID version 4.
- Added: Tests for the path factories, the file backend (including
  symbolic links), ezcWebdavXmlTool and digest authentication that cover
  these fixes.


1.2.1 - Saturday 24 October 2026
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

- Fixed: PROPFIND, LOCK and property output work on PHP 8.
- Fixed: Locks show in PROPFIND, an empty PROPFIND body asks for all
  properties, lock refreshes declare their state.
- Fixed: The component runs on PHP 8.1 to 8.5 without deprecation notices.
- Added: Regression tests for the lock plugin, property escaping and the
  output result on PHP 8.
- Updated: Published as se7enxweb/zetacomponents-webdav, replacing
  zetacomponents/webdav.


1.2 - Saturday 27 September 2014
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

- Updated: Moving copyright information to NOTICE files.
- Updated color scheme of architecture diagram to suite Apache Zeta Components website
- Fixed: Missing file level doc blocks with license in the Webdav component.
- Fixed: Updated copyright dates in NOTICE files.
- Remove custom test runner.
- Fixed autoloading with Composer
- Fixed issue #15922: The default lock timeout in ezcWebdavFileBackend is not
  2 seconds. After this time, a hanging lock will automatically be released.
  This timeout can now be configured through the new option
  ezcWebdavFileBackendOptions->lockTimeout.
- Fixed issue #16034: The permissions on the lock file in ezcWebdavFileBackend
  are now properly checked before a lock is acquired.
- Fixed issue #16194: Files displayed URL encoded in WebDAV clients.
- Fixed issue #16201: Introduced new Nautilus compatible transport class to
  fix client specific issues.


1.1.3 - Monday 09 November 2009
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

- Fixed issue #15430: Dead property retrieval works correctly now in
  ezcWebdavFileBackend.
- Fixed issue #15431: Fixed detection of HTTP/HTTPS in
  ezcWebdavAutomaticPathFactory.
- Fixed issue #15434: Corrected error in example code.
- Fixed issue #15477: Using the property storage file name in the file
  back-end path works now properly.


1.1.2 - Tuesday 01 September 2009
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

- Fixed issue #15368: Corrected and enhanced documentation of ezcWebdavServer
  regarding configuration handling.


1.1.1 - Monday 08 June 2009
